# Pinned llama.cpp commit this repo's heretic-eval harness is built against.
# The harness touches semi-internal llama.cpp APIs (cb_eval, adapter init)
# that change between upstream commits — check out this exact commit before
# building, or expect to re-validate.
# NOTE: the harness itself lives at examples/heretic-eval/ inside the
# llama.cpp tree as a local (untracked) addition on top of this commit.
#
# The gigachat35 arch additionally requires llama.cpp PR #25342 (GigaChat 3.5
# model support + MoE expert offload/caching, --moe-cache-mib) applied on top
# of this commit; it was still unmerged at the time of validation.
#
# Build-stack rule: compile AND link against ONE consistent CUDA toolkit.
# Mixing e.g. CUDA-13 headers with the system cudart-12 at runtime silently
# misreads cudaDeviceProp fields (smpbo becomes garbage) and poisons every
# MoE mm_ids_helper launch with "CUDA error: invalid argument".
